    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and all its tests pass. The build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization for owner creation. The change:\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `OwnerAddress.java` (`rest/function/owner/`), mirroring the existing `OwnerTelephone`/`OwnerEmail` helpers. Its `normalize(String)` trims and collapses whitespace to single spaces, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). A null/whitespace-only value normalizes to the empty string.\n\n**Three call sites updated:**\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 normalizes the address and writes it back onto the request *before* the required-field check, so the check rejects an address that is blank after normalization (400), and the normalized value is what gets stored and returned.\n- `EnsureHouseholdUnique` \u2014 household duplicate detection now compares addresses via `OwnerAddress.normalize` (last name still compared case-insensitively as before).\n- `AssignHouseholdId` \u2014 the shared household-id matching and derivation now use the normalized address form.\n\nBecause `ValidateOwnerFields` republishes the normalized DTO through the pipeline, `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner` persist the normalized value and the `GET` response returns it.\n\nAll tests green: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 covering whitespace/case normalization (`  12  main  st ` \u2192 `12 MAIN STREET`), abbreviation expansion (`7 elm ave` \u2192 `7 ELM AVENUE`), and blank-after-normalize rejection (`   ` \u2192 400).",
